1
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:11,637
Stop!!

2
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:28,237
<i>What just happened?</i>

3
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,537
I'm so sorry, Big Brother...

4
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:38,288
Because of me, you...

5
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,291
It's not your fault, Sarah.
Don't worry about it.

6
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:44,419
When I felt like,
I wanted to save you,

7
00:00:44,545 --> 00:00:46,588
fire shot out of my body.

8
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:49,758
Am I sick?

9
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,885
You're not sick, Sarah!

10
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:53,762
<i>Damn it...</i>

11
00:00:53,929 --> 00:00:56,223
<i>What is happening to her?</i>

12
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:01,311
What's going to happen to me?

13
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:06,400
I'm scared, Big Brother!
I'm so scared!

14
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:12,197
No matter what happens,
I'll protect you.

15
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,741
Don't worry, Sarah.

16
00:01:18,287 --> 00:01:19,413
Big Brother!

17
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:22,207
Big Brother!

18
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,334
S-Sarah!

19
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,628
Big Brother!

20
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,464
Sarah!

21
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:32,509
Big Brother!

22
00:01:39,141 --> 00:01:40,934
Big Brother...

23
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:43,020
S-Sarah?

24
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:49,358
Why didn't you save me?

25
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,904
You promised
you would protect me!

26
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:07,919
<i>Damn it...
That same dream again.</i>

27
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:58,905
EPISODE 7
CROWING OVER A FEATHER

28
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:19,676
I want to play in the sand too!

29
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:25,098
Piyoko, Keiji's having a sand bath.

30
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:25,974
Huh?

31
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:30,645
Chickens sand bathe to remove bugs
and impurities from our feathers.

32
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:34,608
The same way humans bathe
to stay clean and healthy.

33
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,067
Oh...

34
00:04:36,193 --> 00:04:39,112
However, I opt for
a more sophisticated method.

35
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:42,949
I use this!
Bug spray for female chickens!

36
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:47,329
An elegant woman must opt
for an elegant solution!

37
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:48,997
Oh...

38
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:53,627
Uh, excuse me...

39
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:56,963
Are you the chickens
who fight against Demons?

40
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:58,507
How do you know that?

41
00:04:58,590 --> 00:04:59,549
I knew it!

42
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,384
Whoa! Awesome!

43
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:03,178
We've seen you
on the human's phones.

44
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:05,597
You're even famous
in the pigeon world!

45
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:09,684
We're seeing them in real lfe!
They're so cool!

46
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:11,978
Um, If you say so...

47
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:13,855
<i>This is kind of making me blush...</i>

48
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:17,025
Oh! Why don't we ask him?

49
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:19,194
What?
There's no way he'd accept!

50
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,737
It seems like he's with his family.

51
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:22,697
It won't hurt to ask...

52
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,619
Uh, would you be interested...

53
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,038
...in joining us for a group date?

54
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,498
A group date?

55
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:34,501
You mean one of those
things human males and females do?

56
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:37,379
Yes! They're very popular
in the pigeon world right now.

57
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,089
P-Popular?!

58
00:05:39,548 --> 00:05:40,632
<i>I had no idea...</i>

59
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:44,636
Our third had to go on
a last-minute carrier pigeon job,

60
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,012
so he just canceled.

61
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:48,098
So we were wondering
if you'd be interested

62
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:49,266
in joining us in his place?

63
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,308
Me?

64
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:52,978
Honestly, I 'm not interested in pigeons.

65
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:54,729
Please, just come with us!

66
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,066
With you there,
there will be so much to talk about!

67
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,735
Plus, I think the ladies would
love to talk to a hero!

68
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:03,029
Please, just come for a little bit!

69
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:08,410
Sounds like fun.
Keiji, you should go with them.

70
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:14,081
W-Well, if you all insist...

71
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,292
I guess I can go
for a little.

72
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:17,544
- Thank you very much!
- Thank you very much!

73
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:25,594
What?!
Why is there a chicken here?

74
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,305
What a bummer.

75
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:30,348
Looks like this meet-up's a dud.

76
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:33,310
This isn't what you promised.

77
00:06:33,435 --> 00:06:35,645
S-Sorry! Huh, that's weird!

78
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:36,938
You don't recognize him?

79
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,900
He's the famous rooster
who fights monsters!

80
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:41,985
- Never heard of him.
- Never heard of him.

81
00:06:42,277 --> 00:06:45,864
Anyways, chickens can't fly.
That's not cool.

82
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:49,618
They go "kokekokko"
and it's kind of weird.

83
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:52,579
What's that dangling from his chin?
Gross!

84
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:57,250
What did you say?!

85
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,461
Hey you!

86
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:01,755
Don't tease the Mister!

87
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,257
Piyoko, calm down.

88
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:05,967
Keiji, listen up.

89
00:07:06,468 --> 00:07:07,468
To be honest,

90
00:07:07,469 --> 00:07:10,764
I can't stand hearing them
slandering us like that.

91
00:07:10,889 --> 00:07:12,641
I'm steaming mad!

92
00:07:13,016 --> 00:07:15,268
It really makes my crown curl!

93
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,979
But Keiji, no violence.

94
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:20,940
This is a group date.
The battlefield is a social one.

95
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:23,401
So we need to woo them
on this date

96
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,820
by showing them
how awesome chickens truly are.

97
00:07:26,071 --> 00:07:28,490
That's how we win.

98
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:33,662
I see.
So it all rests on my shoulders.

99
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:35,246
Leave it to me.

100
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:39,376
My pride as a chicken is
on the line in this battle...

101
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,544
I mean date.

102
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:47,342
I'll use my undeniable appeal and
make them fall in love with me!

103
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,300
Uh...?

104
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,845
Go get 'em, Mister!

105
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:54,306
- <i>Something seems off.
- Go get 'em, Mister! Go get 'em!</i>

106
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:56,267
- <i>I hope he'll be all right.
- Go get 'em, Mister!</i>

107
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,853
Let's start with intros!

108
00:07:59,104 --> 00:08:00,021
I'm Ken!

109
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:01,773
I'm Masa. Nice to meet you.

110
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:05,485
I'm Ann.

111
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:06,653
I'm Seiko.

112
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,530
I'm Marin. Nice to meet you.

113
00:08:10,532 --> 00:08:11,574
My...

114
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:12,909
Name is...

115
00:08:21,543 --> 00:08:23,920
Ah! Keiji!

116
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:27,090
You are so cool, Mister!

117
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,341
Not cool.

118
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:30,009
Cringe.

119
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:31,344
Gross.

120
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:36,975
<i>I should have seen this coming.</i>

121
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:40,854
Wow!

122
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:43,690
Amazing, you're a racing pigeon!

123
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:46,108
We pigeons have
an instinctual sense of direction,

124
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:48,528
so I can fly out a 100 kilometers
and still find my way home.

125
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:51,281
Now's your chance to
show them what you've got!

126
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,074
Uh, okay!

127
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:55,410
Chickens are great too, you know!

128
00:08:56,578 --> 00:08:58,371
We get up early and our voices are loud.

129
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:00,664
That is so annoying in the
morning!

130
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:01,916
It's so loud, huh?

131
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,044
Something else! Something else!

132
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:05,503
We run fast!

133
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:07,255
Flying is faster...

134
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:08,131
Yup.

135
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,632
Doesn't seem too efficient.

136
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:11,342
- I know!
- I know!

137
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:14,763
We have big crowns!

138
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:17,432
Crowns aren't really that necessary!

139
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:21,519
We forget about bad things
in three seconds!

140
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:23,646
I don't think it's just
about the bad things.

141
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:26,399
Ugh. He doesn't seem too smart.

142
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:27,901
I'm a hard pass on a
lack of smarts.

143
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,069
Agreed!

144
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:30,820
This is getting more
and more unbearable.

145
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,530
I feel kind of bad for him.

146
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:35,158
That's enough!

147
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:45,668
I don't care what
you think about chickens.

148
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:49,297
As long as I live a life with pride,
that's all that matters.

149
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:54,427
I'll walk the path I choose.

150
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:56,096
That's all I can do.

151
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:01,267
- So cool!
- So cool!

152
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:05,563
I've never met such a manly bird!

153
00:10:05,647 --> 00:10:08,024
I've been looking for a man
just like him!

154
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,193
If you look close,
he's actually hot.

155
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,778
Huh? What?

156
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:15,990
<i>I...don't really get it...
Is this what they call...</i>

157
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:22,163
<i>A walk-off home run?!</i>

158
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:23,623
Will you go out with me?

159
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:24,499
No, me!

160
00:10:24,541 --> 00:10:26,251
Marry me!

161
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:28,628
- Hey! The Mister is my husband!
- Please!

162
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,132
<i>What is going on here?</i>

163
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:34,884
Well, ya got me here...

164
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:37,762
- Please!
- Hey, marry me!

165
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,307
He's a man whore.

166
00:10:44,269 --> 00:10:46,980
Y-You sold me out!

167
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:51,817
- The worst.
- Scum.

168
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:52,986
Trash.

169
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:54,988
- Too bad.
- What a letdown.

170
00:11:05,915 --> 00:11:10,336
I feel horrible. I'm sorry.
I don't know what came over me earlier.

171
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:12,046
It's nothing.

172
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:14,507
They were just pigeons anyway.

173
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:17,760
<i>What is going on with me?</i>

174
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:18,970
Elizabeth!

175
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,389
Next time I won't forgive you!

176
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:22,599
Got it?!

177
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:33,359
Make sure to keep her safe
next time, okay?

178
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,636
What are you going to do now?

179
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:04,224
Run, Keisuke.

180
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,354
- After him!
- No, wait.

181
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:12,106
Even if we let him go, we have a hostage.

182
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,484
He'll be back
sooner or later.

183
00:12:20,949 --> 00:12:24,285
<i>I'll come back for you, Father!</i>

184
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,704
<i>Please hold on!</i>

185
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:34,254
What are you doing, Elizabeth?

186
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,256
I'm making lunch.

187
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:37,507
Hey!

188
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:40,176
I've seen this fish before!

189
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:43,680
It's the same one
that was on Pop's back!

190
00:12:44,806 --> 00:12:47,308
It's called a carp, Piyoko.

191
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:48,935
Line caught?

192
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,353
Absolutely not.

193
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:55,483
I just sent a current through a location
in the pond where I though carp would be.

194
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,151
Easy, right?

195
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,028
I didn't know you could do that.

196
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,822
Looks like fun!

197
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:02,991
I wanna do that too!

198
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,993
Can I do it too?

199
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:08,079
Hmm...

200
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:11,499
It might be a few months
too soon for you.

201
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:16,671
I can catch a carp too,
you know!

202
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:19,799
I'll use this—

203
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,722
Like I said, it's too soon for you.

204
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:29,684
I'll overlook this for now...

205
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:33,980
<i>Oh! There's something just right
for her to do over there...</i>

206
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,064
Piyoko...

207
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:38,484
Could you please pick me three
dandelion flowers for me over there?

208
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:40,069
I want to add them to the food.

209
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:42,404
Flowers to decorate our food, right?

210
00:13:42,405 --> 00:13:44,115
That's easy peasy!

211
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:48,286
Flowers... flowers...

212
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,998
There are so many flowers,
aren't there?

213
00:13:52,415 --> 00:13:53,249
Huh?

214
00:13:54,042 --> 00:13:57,545
These flowers are small and cute,
just like me!

215
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:59,380
I'll get these!

216
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,800
Those are flowers too, Piyoko...
But...

217
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:07,346
The dandelions that
I wanted you to get are these.

218
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:11,559
I just took a side route

219
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:14,645
and I was going to
get those flowers later on!

220
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:17,356
If you got them already,
then I guess this was all pointless!

221
00:14:22,153 --> 00:14:26,574
The last step is to season it
with salt and pepper, and...

222
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:28,618
...it's done!

223
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:32,205
White fish saute with a
two-tone vegetable sauce,

224
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,623
and a dandelion garnish.

225
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,751
Yay! I love fish!

226
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:38,044
Is it edible?

227
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:39,128
How rude!

228
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:40,963
Cooking is one of my talents,
okay?!

229
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:44,467
<i>I mean, how good can it be?</i>

230
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:51,599
Delicious!!!

231
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:55,311
<i>What is this? The vegetable sauce
perfectly complements the carp,</i>

232
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:59,273
<i>neutralizing the fishiness
while drawing out full-bodied flavor!</i>

233
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:00,900
<i>It tastes just like the time</i>

234
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,569
<i>I ate a grasshopper
and a frog at the same time...</i>

235
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:06,906
<i>and a revolution occured
on my tastebuds! It's better than that!</i>

236
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,909
I'm a genius!

237
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,661
Let's eat!

238
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:12,745
Wait!

239
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:25,758
I have the smallest portion!

240
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:30,263
What?! They're the same size!

241
00:15:30,388 --> 00:15:32,932
Nope! This corner on
this one is missing!

242
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:34,225
Don't be greedy!

243
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:36,310
The only thing small here,
is your character!

244
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:38,271
Just be grateful you're
getting a portion!

245
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:40,398
Give me another half,
then I'll be grateful!

246
00:15:41,858 --> 00:15:43,567
- Hey! Don't mess around!
- Let me eat more!

247
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:45,194
- Absolutely not!
- Let me eat more!

248
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:47,071
Let me eat more!

249
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,865
Let me eat more!

250
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:50,408
Let me eat more!

251
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:54,495
Hey, Mister, I'm not hungry,
so you can have mine!

252
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:55,872
Oh, thank you !!

253
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,083
Huh?

254
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,502
You'd eat a child's portion?!

255
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,670
You scum!

256
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:05,756
So delicious!!

257
00:16:05,882 --> 00:16:07,425
Spit it back out right now!

258
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:08,718
No can do!

259
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,724
So? Any more info
on the White Demon?

260
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,892
No.

261
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:18,769
There's nothing
since his last appearance.

262
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:21,230
I haven't found any new leads since.

263
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:26,152
All we can do right now is head
to where he was last sighted.

264
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:29,280
We might find a clue there.

265
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:33,242
We still have
at least 250 kilometers to go...

266
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:34,327
Huh?

267
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:36,787
Come to think of it...
Where's Piyoko?

268
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,251
What?! Only one bug?

269
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,170
We told you to catch ten,
didn't we?

270
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,880
You messin' with us, huh?!

271
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,174
C-Catching ten is impossible!

272
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,717
Please forgive me!

273
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,470
Is there some reason
why you can't follow my orders?

274
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:56,307
You know what happens now,
don't you?!

275
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,935
Die!

276
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,019
Hold it!

277
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,693
Are you hurt?

278
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:08,778
N-No!

279
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:10,279
Who the hell are you?!

280
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:11,280
Hmph!

281
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,907
Me, you say?

282
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:17,328
I'm "Dutiful Piyoko"!

283
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:21,707
DUTY

284
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:21,582
I live by Pops' credo and
I never let evil off the hook!

285
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,126
<i>My entrance is spot on!</i>

286
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:28,297
So this little chick wants to fight us?

287
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:32,468
Fine. I'm happy to oblige.

288
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:34,845
We're gonna kill you!

289
00:17:50,945 --> 00:17:55,199
Phew! Think twice before
doing anything bad ever again, got it?

290
00:17:56,826 --> 00:18:00,580
Damn it. I'm not done here!

291
00:18:02,290 --> 00:18:04,625
Do it! I dare you!

292
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,711
Kiss my butt!

293
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:11,173
Unforgiveable!

294
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:15,928
You're not getting away with this!

295
00:18:18,973 --> 00:18:19,807
Huh?

296
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:33,362
<i>Demon alert issued.</i>

297
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:36,907
- <i>Demon alert issued.</i>
- Get back here!

298
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,159
<i>Danger.</i>

299
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,870
- <i>Evacuate the area immediately.</i>
- Get back here, you brat!

300
00:18:41,162 --> 00:18:43,623
Stop right now, you brat!

301
00:18:43,998 --> 00:18:47,043
I'm not stopping!

302
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:49,003
Come back here!

303
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:20,618
<i>P-Pops!</i>

304
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:42,181
You're a billion years too green
to face off against me!

305
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:43,557
Huh?!

306
00:20:01,409 --> 00:20:02,326
Was that—?

307
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,913
Are you hurt, Piyoko?

308
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:15,005
Wait... Piyoko?

309
00:20:24,724 --> 00:20:28,144
Why am I so weak?

310
00:20:28,728 --> 00:20:34,191
Why can't I be useful
for the Mister, like Elizabeth?

311
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:37,528
I always need to be saved.

312
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:41,991
<i>Hey, Mister, I'm not hungry
so you can have mine!</i>

313
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,206
<i>I know full well...</i>

314
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:52,376
<i>...that that's all I can offer.</i>

315
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:56,130
<i>I know I'm useless and
nothing more than dead weight.</i>

316
00:20:57,673 --> 00:21:02,303
But I don't want to be that!
I don't want to be a burden to him!

317
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,975
<i>Maybe...</i>

318
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:14,857
<i>...my time with him is coming to an end.</i>

319
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:20,780
Is her stomach upset?

320
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:23,365
I think she might be
depressed about something.

321
00:21:24,325 --> 00:21:25,493
Keiji...

322
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:28,829
I've been a little concerned
about something.

323
00:21:29,330 --> 00:21:32,082
We've been with Piyoko
for about a month now...

324
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:36,879
DUTY

325
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:36,253
But she hasn't grown at all.

326
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:39,340
Any way you look at it,
isn't that strange?

327
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,426
So, you noticed too.

328
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:50,434
Who the hell are you?

329
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,353
I...

330
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:54,563
I finally found you...

331
00:21:55,231 --> 00:21:56,315
Big...

332
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:57,775
... Brother.

333
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:00,277
A-Are you all right?!

334
00:22:02,238 --> 00:22:03,906
<i>W-What did he...</i>

335
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,659
<i>...just say?!</i>

336
00:23:50,012 --> 00:23:54,224
It's finally time for the
Goshikidori Family to make our entrance.

337
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:58,103
But Keisuke, this town feels
dangerous.

338
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:01,482
Next time:
Not All Feathers Hold a Song.

339
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:04,068
Oh, I've located a lady!

340
00:24:04,902 --> 00:24:09,823
FAN ART CONTEST AWARDS

